{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1772833687233,"sessionID":"ses_33ae23cc0ffepRucRBrP1I8Zi5","part":{"id":"prt_cc51e0401001pqXCV77D4xziDb","sessionID":"ses_33ae23cc0ffepRucRBrP1I8Zi5","messageID":"msg_cc51dc4080019Vznxwfrw1wgoH","type":"tool","callID":"call_function_uwyk6iwo7fha_1","tool":"task","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"Explore the codebase to understand the current authentication implementation","description":"Explore auth implementation","prompt":"I need to understand the current authentication implementation for a webui key prompt feature. Please find and analyze:\n\n1. The key modal implementation in index.html (look for key-modal, getKey, saveKey functions)\n2. The authentication logic in api.go (look for checkDashboardAuth, checkAPIAuth, authenticated checks)\n3. The serveClientPage function in api.go \n4. The WebSocket handler in api.go\n5. The config for DashboardKey (in config.go or similar)\n6. Any existing tests related to authentication (pwa_test.go)\n\nFor each file found, note the specific line numbers and what the code does. Be thorough - this is a very thorough exploration.","subagent_type":"explore"},"output":"task_id: ses_33ae1ed23ffek9TDXP6NhhCc0Z (for resuming to continue this task if needed)\n\n<task_result>\nNow I have all the information. Here's a comprehensive analysis of the authentication implementation:\n\n---\n\n## 1. Key Modal Implementation in index.html\n\n**File:** `/home/paule/MAD/server/templates/index.html`\n\n### Key Modal HTML (Lines 250-257)\n```html\n<div class=\"modal-overlay\" id=\"key-modal\">\n    <div class=\"modal\" style=\"max-width:400px\">\n        <h3>Authentication Required</h3>\n        <p style=\"color:#8b949e;margin:0.5rem 0 1rem\">Enter your dashboard key to access client details.</p>\n        <input type=\"password\" id=\"key-input\" placeholder=\"Enter key\" style=\"width:100%;padding:0.75rem;background:#0d1117;border:1px solid #30363d;border-radius:6px;color:#c9d1d9;font-size:1rem;margin-bottom:1rem\">\n        <button onclick=\"saveKey()\">Save Key</button>\n    </div>\n</div>\n```\n\n### getKey() Function (Lines 442-449)\n- Retrieves key from URL query parameter `?key=`\n- If found in URL, stores it in localStorage\n- Also checks localStorage for existing key\n- Returns the key or empty string\n\n### saveKey() Function (Lines 451-459)\n- Gets value from key-input field\n- Trims whitespace\n- Saves to localStorage with key `'mad_key'`\n- Hides modal and reloads page\n\n### Key Auto-Append Logic (Lines 461-489)\n- Automatically appends `?key=` to all client links\n- Handles HTMX requests by adding key to swapped content\n- Shows modal on 401 response errors (HTMX)\n- Shows modal immediately if no key exists and modal exists\n\n### CSS Toggle (Lines 207-208)\n```css\n#dashboard-content { display: none; }\n#dashboard-content.authenticated { display: block; }\n```\nThe `.Authenticated` template variable controls content visibility.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Authentication Logic in api.go\n\n**File:** `/home/paule/MAD/server/api.go`\n\n### checkAPIAuth() Function (Lines 63-82)\n```go\nfunc checkAPIAuth(r *http.Request, apiKey string) bool {\n    if apiKey == \"\" {\n        return true  // No key configured = allow all\n    }\n    // Check ?key= query parameter\n    if r.URL.Query().Get(\"key\") == apiKey {\n        return true\n    }\n    // Check Authorization: Bearer <key>\n    if auth := r.Header.Get(\"Authorization\"); auth != \"\" {\n        if strings.HasPrefix(auth, \"Bearer \") && strings.TrimPrefix(auth, \"Bearer \") == apiKey {\n            return true\n        }\n    }\n    // Check X-API-Key header\n    if r.Header.Get(\"X-API-Key\") == apiKey {\n        return true\n    }\n    return false\n}\n```\n\n### checkDashboardAuth() Function (Lines 84-89)\n```go\nfunc checkDashboardAuth(r *http.Request, dashboardKey string) bool {\n    if dashboardKey == \"\" {\n        return true  // No key configured = allow all\n    }\n    return r.URL.Query().Get(\"key\") == dashboardKey\n}\n```\n\n### Key Differences:\n- **checkAPIAuth**: Supports multiple methods (query param, Bearer token, X-API-Key header)\n- **checkDashboardAuth**: Only checks query parameter `?key=`\n\n---\n\n## 3. serveClientPage Function\n\n**File:** `/home/paule/MAD/server/api.go` (Lines 530-591)\n\n```go\nfunc serveClientPage(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request, hub *Hub, tmpl *template.Template, cfg *Config)\n```\n\n**What it does:**\n- Extracts clientID from URL path `/clients/{id}`\n- Gets client state from hub\n- Extracts `key` from query parameter\n- Handles sub-resources (HTMX fragments):\n  - `/clients/{id}/features` - returns feature stages template\n  - `/clients/{id}/logs` - returns log entries template\n- Renders client.html template with client data\n- **Does NOT perform any authentication check** - it accepts key but doesn't validate it for serving the page\n\n---\n\n## 4. WebSocket Handler\n\n**File:** `/home/paule/MAD/server/api.go` (Lines 278-318)\n\n```go\nmux.HandleFunc(\"/ws\", func(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {\n    // Auth via query param or header\n    authorized := false\n    if cfg.APIKey == \"\" {\n        authorized = true\n    } else {\n        if r.URL.Query().Get(\"api_key\") == cfg.APIKey {\n            authorized = true\n        } else if checkAPIAuth(r, cfg.APIKey) {\n            authorized = true\n        }\n    }\n    if !authorized {\n        writeJSON(w, http.StatusUnauthorized, map[string]string{\"error\": \"unauthorized\"})\n        return\n    }\n    // ... WebSocket upgrade and client registration\n})\n```\n\n**What it does:**\n- Checks if APIKey is configured (empty = allow all)\n- Accepts `?api_key=` query parameter OR standard auth methods\n- Returns 401 if unauthorized\n- Upgrades to WebSocket and registers client with hub\n\n---\n\n## 5. DashboardKey Configuration\n\n**File:** `/home/paule/MAD/server/config.go`\n\n### Config Struct (Lines 10-15)\n```go\ntype Config struct {\n    Port         int\n    APIKey       string\n    DashboardKey string\n    MaxLogLines  int\n}\n```\n\n### Loading DashboardKey (Lines 37-40)\n```go\ncfg.DashboardKey = os.Getenv(\"SERVER_DASHBOARD_KEY\")\nif cfg.DashboardKey == \"\" {\n    log.Println(\"WARNING: SERVER_DASHBOARD_KEY is not set, dashboard is unprotected\")\n}\n```\n\n**Environment variable:** `SERVER_DASHBOARD_KEY`\n\n---\n\n## 6. Authentication Tests in pwa_test.go\n\n**File:** `/home/paule/MAD/server/pwa_test.go`\n\n### TestPWAAssetsNoAuthRequired (Lines 614-643)\n- Tests that PWA assets (manifest.json, icons, sw.js, favicon) are accessible WITHOUT authentication even when DashboardKey and APIKey are set\n\n### TestDashboardRequiresAuthButAssetsDoNot (Lines 645-666)\n- Tests that dashboard (/) requires auth when DashboardKey is set\n- Tests that static assets do NOT require auth\n\n---\n\n## Authentication Flow Summary\n\n| Endpoint | Auth Method | Check Function |\n|----------|-------------|----------------|\n| `/` (dashboard) | `?key=` query param | `checkDashboardAuth` (line 138) |\n| `/clients/{id}` | `?key=` query param | None (accepts but doesn't validate) |\n| `/api/board` | `?key=` query param | `checkDashboardAuth` (line 230) |\n| `/api/clients` | `?key=`, Bearer, X-API-Key | `checkAPIAuth` (line 201) |\n| `/api/clients/{id}/...` | `?key=`, Bearer, X-API-Key | `checkAPIAuth` + `checkDashboardAuth` (varies) |\n| `/ws` | `?api_key=`, Bearer, X-API-Key | Custom (line 282-290) |\n| PWA assets | None | No auth required |\n\nThe `authenticated` template variable (line 138) is calculated as:\n```go\nauthenticated := key != \"\" && (cfg.DashboardKey == \"\" || key == cfg.DashboardKey)\n```\nThis determines whether `.Authenticated` is true in the template, which controls whether dashboard content is shown.\n</task_result>","title":"Explore auth implementation","metadata":{"sessionId":"ses_33ae1ed23ffek9TDXP6NhhCc0Z","model":{"modelID":"minimax/minimax-m2.5","providerID":"kilo"},"truncated":false},"time":{"start":1772833608410,"end":1772833687232}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Let me analyze this feature request and the extensive review feedback to understand what's been tried before and what still needs to be addressed.\n\n## Summary of the Feature:\nThe frontend should display a modal overlay prompting for the API key to allow access to the webui. The key is stored in localStorage for persistence. Without a valid key (either entered or stored), the backend should not send any actual data to the frontend - all content is blocked until authenticated.\n\n## Key Issues from Review Feedback:\n\n1. **CRITICAL: Modal is inside {{if .Authenticated}} block** - The key modal (lines 250-257 in index.html) is inside the {{if .Authenticated}} conditional (line 210), so unauthenticated users see a blank page.\n\n2. **Data leakage** - Backend still fetches all clients and features regardless of auth status, only hiding with CSS. Data is sent to frontend but visually hidden.\n\n3. **Client page auth missing** - serveClientPage (api.go:530) does NOT validate dashboard key at all.\n\n4. **WebSocket gap** - WebSocket handler only validates APIKey, not DashboardKey.\n\n5. **Security concern** - Key passed via query params (?key=) which leaks in logs, URLs, browser history.\n\n6. **No invalid key feedback** - When user enters wrong key, no error message shown.\n\n7. **localStorage unavailable** - No handling for private browsing mode.\n\n8. **Test expects failure** - pwa_test.go:656 expects / to return non-200 when DashboardKey is set.\n\n9. **Logout option** - User asked for logout/clear key option.\n\nLet me explore the codebase to understand the current implementation and what's needed.","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":"0848492c0b213a4e60af3b32f5c0a8f5531f9af169a095262d8dee2bea85f482"}]}}}}
